{"vid":"0zzQ1jth6Cw","source":"0zzQ1jth6Cw.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.1,"txt":"If you've applied for a job recently,"},{"t":1.9,"txt":"there's a growing chance the first person interviewing"},{"t":4.2,"txt":"you isn't a person at all."},{"t":6.2,"txt":"They just said, okay, well,"},{"t":8.4,"txt":"we would like to do a phone interview and we will be"},{"t":10.3,"txt":"calling you at this time."},{"t":11.6,"txt":"And so, at first, I'm like talking like I"},{"t":14.4,"txt":"would to a person and then it clicks in that this is"},{"t":16.8,"txt":"not a person."},{"t":18.2,"txt":"Nearly two-thirds of job seekers surveyed in 2026"},{"t":21.8,"txt":"said they've already been interviewed by AI,"},{"t":24.4,"txt":"a 12% increase from six months prior."},{"t":27.1,"txt":"There are several reasons why employers are leaning"},{"t":29.4,"txt":"into AI to conduct more interviews."},{"t":31.8,"txt":"I think some companies probably are using it as a"},{"t":35.2,"txt":"cost-saving measure if they do not have"},{"t":36.9,"txt":"an in-house recruiter."},{"t":38,"txt":"Employers are also facing a historic surge in job"},{"t":40.6,"txt":"applications, with the number of U.S."},{"t":42.5,"txt":"applicants for each open role doubling since the"},{"t":45.1,"txt":"spring of 2022, according to LinkedIn."},{"t":47.5,"txt":"I think the biggest reason would be time saved."},{"t":50.3,"txt":"One thing it's important to remember is that throughout"},{"t":53.6,"txt":"the ups and downs of the economic and just sort of"},{"t":57.3,"txt":"hiring climate over the last six or so years,"},{"t":60.3,"txt":"what used to be really robust recruiting teams have"},{"t":63.9,"txt":"been cut down quite a bit to be sometimes even just 1 or"},{"t":66.6,"txt":"2 people, depending on the size of the company."},{"t":68.7,"txt":"And with the influx of applications,"},{"t":71.7,"txt":"there are a lot of great folks out there,"},{"t":73.6,"txt":"and for some companies, I imagine it is nearly"},{"t":76.5,"txt":"impossible to screen all of their qualified applicants."},{"t":79.8,"txt":"So what does an AI interview actually look like?"},{"t":82.8,"txt":"The process varies depending on the software the employer"},{"t":85.4,"txt":"uses, but the system usually starts with a brief"},{"t":87.9,"txt":"introduction, then asks a series of questions based on"},{"t":90.5,"txt":"the job description, recording your answers along"},{"t":92.9,"txt":"the way. Afterward, the software sends the"},{"t":95.1,"txt":"hiring manager the information they might need,"},{"t":97.5,"txt":"which could include a short summary of the conversation,"},{"t":100.6,"txt":"a score showing how closely a candidate matched the job"},{"t":103.2,"txt":"requirements, an assessment of their performance,"},{"t":105.9,"txt":"and a final overall score or ranking."},{"t":108.3,"txt":"The hiring manager then ultimately decides who moves"},{"t":111,"txt":"to the next round, which usually involves a"},{"t":113.5,"txt":"human-to-human conversation."},{"t":115.3,"txt":"While it all sounds very convenient for the"},{"t":117.1,"txt":"employers, AI interviews still have some obvious"},{"t":119.5,"txt":"limitations."},{"t":120.7,"txt":"AI interview tools really stink at asking follow-up"},{"t":124.9,"txt":"questions because LLMs are coded on what they expect"},{"t":129.3,"txt":"the next word to be."},{"t":130.6,"txt":"And so what I've seen in those systems recently is"},{"t":134,"txt":"that people will use gibberish with the tool,"},{"t":137.5,"txt":"and then the tool will ask a follow-up question,"},{"t":139.9,"txt":"but they ask it with the gibberish embedded because"},{"t":143,"txt":"it doesn't have the intelligence to ask a good"},{"t":146.2,"txt":"next question."},{"t":147.3,"txt":"What I found is if you're pausing to think and you're"},{"t":150.4,"txt":"letting a moment really sink in, or you're processing the"},{"t":153,"txt":"question and you're letting it go,"},{"t":155.5,"txt":"it will interrupt or move you straight onto the next"},{"t":158,"txt":"question without giving you the opportunity to think on"},{"t":160.6,"txt":"it, noodle a little bit, and then give an answer,"},{"t":162.9,"txt":"or take 30 seconds and restate what you were trying"},{"t":166,"txt":"to say. It really does a bad job of the human element of"},{"t":169.6,"txt":"the interviewing process."},{"t":171.2,"txt":"In response, some job seekers are deciding the"},{"t":173.6,"txt":"trade-off simply isn't worth it."},{"t":175.8,"txt":"They're giving me an opportunity to speak and"},{"t":178.5,"txt":"record my answers."},{"t":180.2,"txt":"But if I hesitated in any sort of way,"},{"t":184,"txt":"the recording would end and then they would move on to"},{"t":187.1,"txt":"the next question. So I never really ever got to"},{"t":189.8,"txt":"formulate any sort of answer."},{"t":192.7,"txt":"But sometimes the concerns go beyond a frustrating"},{"t":195.6,"txt":"candidate experience."},{"t":197.3,"txt":"Researchers have also warned that AI hiring tools can"},{"t":200.1,"txt":"reinforce bias, and complaints against some"},{"t":202.4,"txt":"software providers allege discrimination based on"},{"t":204.9,"txt":"factors like age, race, and disability."},{"t":207.3,"txt":"I couldn't even record the video because I have a"},{"t":212.2,"txt":"condition called nystagmus, and that causes involuntary"},{"t":217.1,"txt":"movement of my eyeballs."},{"t":219.1,"txt":"When I'm talking, my eyeballs are continuously"},{"t":222.9,"txt":"moving. Every time it would stop the video and say,"},{"t":227,"txt":"please look straight ahead and speak."},{"t":232.3,"txt":"I couldn't finish the video."},{"t":233.7,"txt":"I had to stop it, you know?"},{"t":235.5,"txt":"And I thought that that was,"},{"t":238.1,"txt":"that was probably like the lowest point in my search"},{"t":242.8,"txt":"because it was just demoralizing that,"},{"t":246.1,"txt":"you know, I couldn't be treated like a human being"},{"t":250,"txt":"to have a conversation with."},{"t":251.9,"txt":"According to a recent survey,"},{"t":253.7,"txt":"nearly 4 in 10 U.S."},{"t":255.3,"txt":"candidates say they've already withdrawn from a"},{"t":257.5,"txt":"hiring process because it included an AI interview."},{"t":260.6,"txt":"12% of those surveyed said they would withdraw their"},{"t":263.2,"txt":"application if one were required."},{"t":265.1,"txt":"That's notable in a tight labor market that currently"},{"t":267.4,"txt":"gives employers much of the leverage."},{"t":269.5,"txt":"I have spoken with people who have varying degrees of"},{"t":272.7,"txt":"positive to negative interactions,"},{"t":274.3,"txt":"but I think the one through line that it really is"},{"t":276.9,"txt":"lacking in that human experience."},{"t":279.7,"txt":"I think having an interview in a digital environment is"},{"t":284.6,"txt":"one of those things that we human beings think we're"},{"t":287.5,"txt":"really good at, but I actually don't think"},{"t":290.1,"txt":"we are, because there are these social and emotional"},{"t":292.8,"txt":"components that come up when a human is talking to a"},{"t":296.1,"txt":"machine, right? There's no one there to say,"},{"t":298.3,"txt":"it's okay, don't be nervous."},{"t":300.7,"txt":"And broadly, we also have some of that performance"},{"t":304.7,"txt":"anxiety of how do I show up my best when I don't have a"},{"t":308.1,"txt":"person on the other side to nod or confirm that I'm"},{"t":311.7,"txt":"giving them the answer that I need."},{"t":313.5,"txt":"And you know, the endurance of giving your"},{"t":316.4,"txt":"best answer over and over again without a human"},{"t":318.8,"txt":"interacting is something that we as a society"},{"t":321.3,"txt":"aren't really good at."},{"t":324.1,"txt":"For job seekers who do decide to go through with an"},{"t":326.4,"txt":"AI interview, here are a few tips."},{"t":328.6,"txt":"So I recommend you always start by being very,"},{"t":331.9,"txt":"very clear and saying yes or no."},{"t":334.4,"txt":"Yes, I did this."},{"t":335.9,"txt":"No, I have not done that."},{"t":337.6,"txt":"And you need to answer that explicitly,"},{"t":340.1,"txt":"all right? No need for nuance here."},{"t":342.4,"txt":"Remember, it's a bot on the other side."},{"t":344.1,"txt":"Really enunciate."},{"t":345.7,"txt":"Remember that you're talking to a language model and you"},{"t":348.7,"txt":"can ask for restating more clear answers,"},{"t":351.9,"txt":"an example of what it's saying."},{"t":353.9,"txt":"A lot of them have these conversational elements"},{"t":357.1,"txt":"built into it."},{"t":358.1,"txt":"Candidates are really struggling with AI"},{"t":360.9,"txt":"interviewing because they think it's an all-new skill,"},{"t":364,"txt":"or that they should be applying a different"},{"t":366.4,"txt":"methodology to be successful in that environment than"},{"t":369.4,"txt":"they typically would in a traditional interview"},{"t":371.5,"txt":"environment. The truth is, and I find myself telling"},{"t":374.1,"txt":"people this a lot, is that the same rules"},{"t":377.5,"txt":"apply. You just need to communicate about your"},{"t":380.3,"txt":"experience in a slightly different way in an AI"},{"t":383.5,"txt":"environment than you do with a person,"},{"t":385.4,"txt":"because there's not a person to fill in all of the gaps"},{"t":388.7,"txt":"that you don't mention explicitly."},{"t":390.3,"txt":"Employers are hoping AI can deliver on speed and scale"},{"t":393.4,"txt":"in hiring, but as applicants push back against an"},{"t":396.1,"txt":"increasingly automated process,"},{"t":397.9,"txt":"companies may have to find a balance between efficiency"},{"t":400.5,"txt":"and maintaining the connection that"},{"t":401.8,"txt":"candidates still value."}],"words":[{"t":0.08,"w":"If"},{"t":0.08,"w":"you've"},{"t":0.08,"w":"applied"},{"t":0.08,"w":"for"},{"t":0.08,"w":"a"},{"t":0.08,"w":"job"},{"t":0.08,"w":"recently,"},{"t":1.92,"w":"there's"},{"t":1.92,"w":"a"},{"t":1.92,"w":"growing"},{"t":1.92,"w":"chance"},{"t":1.